# kind | name | source (on-disk LICENSE path for shards; for clib/runtime, an
# SPDX id of licenses-spdx/, or the path of the library's own license file)
#
# Only what the released binary actually embeds: ameba and spectator are
# development dependencies and never end up in it. Add a `shard` line here for
# every runtime dependency added to shard.yml — nothing checks that for you,
# and a missing notice in a redistributed static binary is precisely the fault
# this file exists to prevent.
#
# CONFIRMED on 2026-11-18 against the link line of this very binary, in
# alpine:3.24 with Alpine's crystal 1.20.3 (the base of the image
# crystalreleaser generates for the linux builds):
#   -lssl -lcrypto -lz -lpcre2-8 -pthread -lgc -ldl  (+ musl, libgcc)
# openssl comes from HTTP::Client (TLS to PagerDuty). Versions and licenses as
# apk records them in that image: openssl 3.5.9 Apache-2.0, pcre2 10.49
# BSD-3-Clause, zlib 1.4 Zlib, musl 1.2.6 MIT, gc 8.2.12 Boehm-GC. The darwin
# binaries link Homebrew's openssl@4 (Apache-2.0) statically, and libgc and
# pcre2 from the compiler mise installs; zlib and libiconv come from macOS
# itself. Check the link line again when a stdlib module is added (yaml, xml,
# big and compress each bring a library of their own) or the image moves.
#
# MIT, BSD-3-Clause and zlib require the copyright notice to be reproduced,
# and their SPDX text only has a blank there: those three libraries embed their
# own license file, taken from their sources at the versions above (the same
# files as crystalreleaser's, which links the same libraries):
#   pcre2    LICENCE.md  github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2  tag pcre2-10.49
#   zlib     LICENSE     github.com/madler/zlib         tag v1.4
#   musl     COPYRIGHT   git.musl-libc.org/cgit/musl    tag v1.2.6
shard   | baked_file_system | lib/baked_file_system/LICENSE
shard   | watch             | lib/watch/LICENSE
clib    | openssl           | Apache-2.0
clib    | pcre2             | licenses-upstream/pcre2.txt
clib    | zlib              | licenses-upstream/zlib.txt
clib    | boehm-gc          | Boehm-GC
clib    | musl              | licenses-upstream/musl.txt
clib    | libgcc            | GCC-runtime-exception
runtime | crystal           | Apache-2.0
project | icinga-pagerduty  | LICENSE
